    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0110" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg30"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Bryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 241.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 318, of the 2d instant, reporting the sack of an American Baptist church by
                    a Catholic mob at Nictheroy and your unofficial conference with the president of
                    the State, during which you discussed the case.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that the Department approves your course thus far, and
                    will be glad to learn of the further developments of the case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
